s and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "South Dakota sits well to the right of the nation, with a partisan lean of roughly fifteen points toward Republicans, and it has backed the Republican presidential nominee in every recent cycle. The 2028 race is an open contest with no incumbent on the ballot, and the Democratic nominee would need a substantial national swing to put the state in play.\n\nNo public polls of the state, expert ratings, fundraising figures, or market prices are available for this race, so the outlook rests on the state's underlying partisan fundamentals. Those fundamentals point to a comfortable Republican win, with the Democratic nominee's path depending on an unusually large national environment shift rather than anything specific to South Dakota. The race is rated Likely Republican, short of safe only because direct polling evidence is absent.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0482, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0894, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0882, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0848, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0844, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0865, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0843, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0921, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.078, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0848, "margin": -15.0}]}